# Study outputs are generated by run-arm.sh / judge-results.sh — not tracked by default.
# The harness INPUTS (prompts.json, answer-key.md, scoring-sheet.csv) and transcripts/README.md
# stay tracked. Commit final AE-provenance transcripts deliberately with `git add -f` if desired.
results-*.csv
transcripts/*.jsonl
transcripts/*.jsonl.err
transcripts/*.answer.txt
transcripts/*.judge.txt

# EXCEPTION — the multi-judge robustness pass under robustness/ IS tracked. Re-deriving it
# costs four judged passes over the 248 saved answers on two paid services, so unlike the
# primary judge's output it is not cheaply reproducible; the paper's judge-strength claim
# (Section VII-A) rests on these files, and the artifact bundle copies from git's index, so
# anything untracked here would be missing from the Zenodo deposit as well. Both kinds are
# small: 4 CSVs at ~18 KB each and 496 rationales totalling ~79 KB.
!robustness/**/results-*.csv
!robustness/**/*.judge.txt
